--
N5008 [ptr.launder]: std::launder(p) returns a pointer to the object at the
address p represents; GCC and Clang implement it as the builtin
`__builtin_launder', which returns its argument (value-wise).  The front
end does not know the builtin ("symbol '__builtin_launder' is unknown").
libc++'s `std::__launder' (new:337) is exactly `return __builtin_launder(__p)'
and is dropped for the map node value type in cpp20_map_basic_libcxx
(round-163 audit); libstdc++'s std::launder uses the same builtin.
Header-free.  Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51 fails the same way).
